            <ArticleTitle>[Lumbar pain and bilateral adrenal masses].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>262-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/S1575-0922(09)71409-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Many problems may arise when defining whether adrenal lesions are primary to the adrenal glands or represent other tissue, whether they are benign or malignant and whether they are functioning or nonfunctioning. Adrenal imaging complements the clinical and hormonal evaluation of these patients. We present a patient with lumbar pain and bilateral adrenal masses.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
